'''amenorrhea, amenorrhœa''' (a-men-ọ̄-rē′ä̤), ''n.'' [NL. ''amenorrhœa'', < Gr. ἀ- priv. + μήν, month (pl. μῆνες, menses), + ῥοία, a flow, < ῥεῖν, flow.] A suppression of menses, especially from other causes than age or pregnancy.

'''amenorrheal, amenorrhœal''' (a-men-ọ̄-rē′a̤l), ''a.'' Pertaining to or produced by amenorrhea: as, ''amenorrheal'' insanity.

'''amenorrheic, amenorrhœic''' (a-men-ọ̄-rē′ik), ''a.'' [< ''amenorrhea''.] Same as ''amenorrheal''.

